---
const { base = '' } = Astro.props;
---

<main id="main" class="article-page">
  <a class="back-link" href={`${base}/blog/`}>
    ← All writing
  </a>
  <header class="article-header">
    <span class="eyebrow">Typography specimen</span>
    <h1>
      A space for
      <br />
      <em>longer thoughts.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="article-deck">
      A reading sample to compare the five designs. This is interface
      demonstration content, not an article or opinion by Erfan.
    </p>
    <p class="article-meta">
      Design preview <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> September 2026
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="sample-notice">
      <strong>Development sample.</strong> This page is available only in local
      development and is excluded from production builds.
    </p>
    <h2>Room to read</h2>
    <p>
      This paragraph demonstrates the width and rhythm of a longer article.
      Comfortable line lengths, clear headings, and generous spacing give the
      text room to breathe on both a small screen and a large one.
    </p>
    <p>
      A future article could include a technical explanation, a project
      retrospective, or a personal observation. Its actual words will come from
      Erfan’s writing.
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      A short quotation has its own space, without interrupting the flow of the
      page.
    </blockquote>
    <h2>A little code</h2>
    <p>
      Technical writing sometimes needs examples. This one shows a small, typed
      function:
    </p>
    <pre><code>type Greeting = &#123; name: string &#125;;

function greet(&#123; name &#125;: Greeting) &#123;
  return `Hello, $&#123;name&#125;.`;
&#125;</code></pre>
    <h2>The details matter</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Headings establish a clear outline.</li>
      <li>Links remain recognizable and keyboard accessible.</li>
      <li>Code scrolls within its own container on narrow screens.</li>
    </ul>
    <hr />
    <p>
      That’s the end of the sample.{' '}
      <a href={`${base}/blog/`}>Return to writing</a> or{' '}
      <a href="/designs/">compare another design</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</main>
